d_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-12T12:44:42Z","updated_at":"2023-08-12T18:36:10Z","body":"~~It might be more composable for the \"restricted middleware\" to require just `T` instead of `Context & T` so that earlier middlewares can override parts of `Context` if the \"restricted middleware\" does not need it~~\r\n\r\n~~also, passing in a runtime schema (e.g. Zod schema) is not strictly necessary if `requires()` would accept an explicit generic like `t.middleware.requires<{ bar: string }>()(handler)` but I dunno which is better~~\r\n\r\n~~there's also maybe a better idea hidden here where, since the middleware can define what it needs from `ctx`, it doesn't necessarily need to be created using `t.middleware` at all, i.e. some kind of `independentMiddleware<{ bar: string }>()` type thing that tRPC instances can then use if they can provide a context that satisfies the type argument.~~\r\n\r\nEDIT:\r\n\r\nseems like this \"standalone middleware\" approach actually works, will commit something once i clean it up","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1675896572/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1676029379","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/4713#issuecomment-1676029379","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/4713","id":1676029379,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5j5i3D","user":{"login":"jussisaurio","id":22619982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5OTgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22619982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio","html_url":"https://github.com/jussisaurio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio